node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
*.tmp
*.bak
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Python bytecode caches: `files` in package.json ships python/, so a stray
# __pycache__ would be packaged into the plugin on install.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Local scratch used by scripts/test-host.mjs (fake $DSH_HOME)
.test-home/

# Runtime output of the inference worker when pointed at the checkout
python/out/
venv/
.pytest_cache/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Audio assets: block everything, allow exactly one reviewed directory.
#
# Voice presets normally live in the plugin's DATA directory
# (`$DSH_HOME/tts-speakout/voices/<id>/`), not in this package, so they are
# outside version control by construction. These rules are the belt-and-braces
# guard: cloned reference audio frequently carries third-party copyright (game
# or anime voice samples, for instance) and must never be redistributed.
#
# The `!assets/**` negation is what lets a reviewed, freely licensed default
# voice ship. It is written against the `assets/` DIRECTORY rather than as
# `!**/*.wav`, because gitignore wildcards do not cross `/` — `!**/*.wav` would
# silently match nothing and the default voice would stay ignored.
#
# Only freely licensed material (CC0 / public domain / CC-BY) may go in assets/.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Audio assets: blocked outright, with NO exception.
#
# This plugin ships **no voice material at all**. Voice presets live in the
# plugin's DATA directory (`$DSH_HOME/tts-speakout/voices/<id>/`), created by the
# user importing their own reference clip, so they are outside version control by
# construction and never travel with the plugin.
#
# The blanket rules below are therefore a hard guard rather than a formality:
# cloned reference audio very often carries third-party copyright (game or anime
# voice samples, for instance). During development this repo was deliberately
# kept free of any such file, and that must stay true for anyone who forks it.
#
# If a freely licensed default voice is ever added on purpose, ship it under an
# explicit `assets/` directory AND add the matching un-ignore rules together
# with its licence/attribution file — never widen these rules "just in case".
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.wav
*.mp3
*.flac
*.m4a
*.ogg
*.aac
*.opus

# Scratch locations that must never be committed: candidate research, downloaded
# corpora, screening tables, and per-candidate metadata.
voice-scout/
voice-candidates/
voices/
ref_audio/
models/
